From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 11:57:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] mtld3d: SubmitTimings is 8-aligned on i686 Linux too

Its offsets are the same on every target (u64s only), but its own
alignment test (align 8, the i686 PE side's) failed on i686 Linux, whose
u64 aligns to 4: align(8), as the crate's other boundary structs say.

Assisted-by: Claude Code: claude-opus-5-5
---
 mtld3d/unix/shared/src/perf.rs | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mtld3d/unix/shared/src/perf.rs b/mtld3d/unix/shared/src/perf.rs
index 7f705edd..227ba979 100644
--- a/mtld3d/unix/shared/src/perf.rs
+++ b/mtld3d/unix/shared/src/perf.rs
@@ -205,7 +205,7 @@ impl Default for GpuBusy {
 /// entries are the command buffers of this device that completed since the
 /// previous submission reported, whichever frame they belong to, so each
 /// completion is reported exactly once.
-#[repr(C)]
+#[repr(C, align(8))]
 pub struct SubmitTimings {
     /// Encoding the frame-leading blits, in whichever buffer carries them.
     pub leading_blits_ns: u64,
-- 
